se,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"eBay Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates marketplace platforms that connect buyers and sellers in the United States, the United Kingdom, China, Germany, and internationally. Its marketplace platform includes its online marketplace at ebay.com, off-platform businesses, and the eBay suite of mobile apps. The company's platforms enable users to list, sell, buy, and pay various products. The company was founded in 1995 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jamie J. Iannone | CEO, President & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $902K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $117K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["eBay Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $49.8B market cap on $11.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.96\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 226% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.2618026814455754},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $31.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Is eBay (EBAY) Down 4.7% Since Last Earnings Report?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036681/why-is-ebay-ebay-down-4-7-since-last-earnings-report?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3036681","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795793424.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Online marketplace stocks Q3 teardown: eBay vs the rest","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/ebay/news/earnings/online-marketplace-stocks-q3-teardown-ebay-vs-the-rest","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795750362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Can eBay (NASDAQ:EBAY) Turn Attention Into Lasting Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/retail/can-ebay-nasdaqebay-turn-attention-into-lasting-growth","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795720620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's How Much $100 Invested In eBay 10 Years Ago Would Be Worth Today","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/63658517/here-s-how-much-100-invested-ebay-10-years-ago-would-be-worth-today","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795646715.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"eBay CEO Jamie Iannone Executes Sale of 35,728 Shares on November 23-24, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/ebay-ceo-jamie-iannone-executes-sale-of-35728-shares-on-november-23-24-2026","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795626659.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"eBay CTO Mazen Rawashdeh Executes 38,288 Stock Options and Sells 40,710 Shares Under 10b5-1 Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemed